                <pb facs="ho_d9-1" n="1" xml:id="ho_d9-1"/>

                <head>HO–9. Editorial Note</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1959-07-12"
                            >July 12, 1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On July 12, 1959, Armando Velásquez Cerrato, the former Chief of Staff of the
                    Honduran Armed Forces, attempted once again to overthrow the government of
                    President Villeda Morales, launching a full scale revolt in Tegucigalpa with the
                    assistance of disloyal police and military units. The bulk of the Honduran Armed
                    Forces remained loyal to President Villeda and acted successfully to crush the
                    revolt and to force Col. Velásquez to seek asylum in the Costa Rican Embassy.
                    Documentation on this incident is in Department of State file 715.00.</p>
            </div>
